  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Widespread soaking rain expected\nThursday. Some drought relief is possible, though flooding is \nnot expected. Showery conditions continue into Saturday.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nAn area of rain will begin to expand eastward across the \nforecast area tonight in advance of an occluded front. A \ndisturbance moving around an upper low across Quebec province \nwill help support a developing low along the front Thursday. \nRain will occur regionwide Thursday, developing from west to \neast after midnight tonight and reaching the New Brunswick \nborder around or shortly after dawn. It will be a steady light\nto possibly moderate rain much of the day Thursday, with only a\nfew breaks in the rain here and there. The developing low \npressure will move east along the Downeast coast Thursday \nevening. Rain chances will begin to diminish late Thursday \nafternoon in western portions of the area, and Thursday night \nfurther east toward the New Brunswick border. Fog is expected\nfor some areas later tonight and again on Thursday night. With\nthe rain during the day Thursday, hilltops will likely be socked\nin with fog as well. Not anticipating dense fog at this time, \nbut will monitor.\n\nThe surface low exits across the Maritimes Friday, with a trof \nextending back across the forecast area, while the upper low \nbegins to move south across the region. Showers will persist \nacross the region Friday, with the better chances across \nnorthern areas. Could also have the slight chance of a \nthunderstorm Friday afternoon particularly in central and \nNorthwest areas. The surface/upper lows vertically stack across \nthe Maritimes Friday night into Saturday, slowing the movement \nof the system. A disturbance moving around the Maritimes system \nwill rotate across the region Saturday. Shower chances will \npersist Friday night into Saturday. The system then exits \nSaturday night into Sunday. The entire forecast area should \nreceive a soaking rain later Wednesday night into Thursday \nnight. Generally expect rainfall totals of a half to three \nquarters of an inch across much of the forecast area Wednesday \nnight into Saturday, with areas of up to around an inch.",
